IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income Tax Act, 2000, s 34(8): the duty of a person receiving the income supplement to
-- tell the Minister of National Revenue about a change. Kept apart from nl-pit.l4 because it needs dates (daydate), which
-- slows type-checking of everything that imports it.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `s 34(8) -- telling the Minister of National Revenue about a change`

-- s 34(8): "An individual shall notify the Minister of National Revenue of the occurrence of any of the following events
-- before the end of the month following the month in which the event occurs (a) the individual ceases to be an eligible
-- individual; (b) a person becomes or ceases to be the individual's qualified relation; and (c) a person ceases to be a
-- qualified dependant of the individual, otherwise than because of attaining the age of 19 years."
DECLARE `s 34(8) event` IS ONE OF
    `I stopped being an eligible individual`
    `someone became or stopped being my qualified relation`
    `someone stopped being my qualified dependant, other than by turning 19`
    `a qualified dependant turned 19`

GIVEN `event` IS A `s 34(8) event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event must be notified` IF
    CONSIDER `event`
    WHEN `a qualified dependant turned 19` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "before the end of the month following the month in which the event occurs": the last day on which notice is in time
-- is the last day of the following month.
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the month following` `the day of the event` MEANS
    BRANCH IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` EQUALS 12 THEN Date 31 1 (DATE_YEAR `the day of the event` PLUS 1)
           OTHERWISE Date (`Days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the event`)) (DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the event`)

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the Minister of National Revenue`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Minister of National Revenue of the event`

-- The duty, counted in days from the day of the event to the last day of the following month.
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to notify the change` `the day of the event` MEANS
    PARTY `the individual`
    MUST  `notify the Minister of National Revenue of the event`
    WITHIN (`the last day of the month following` `the day of the event`) MINUS `the day of the event`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "the change was not notified before the end of the month following the month in which it occurred (s 34(8))"
